  <credit page="1">
    <credit-type>title</credit-type>
    <credit-words default-x="595.44" default-y="1626.67" justify="center" valign="top" font-size="24">Peace, Love, and Unity I</credit-words>
  </credit>
  <credit page="1">
    <credit-type>subtitle</credit-type>
    <credit-words default-x="595.44" default-y="1569.97" justify="center" valign="top" font-size="14">A 200+ National Anthem Medley
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>     
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-style="italic" font-family="Segoe Script" font-size="12"> "While I was browsing through information of national anthems on Wikipedia.org.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>I was curious.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>'What if I combined all the National Anthems in to one?' I said to myself.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>And thus, Peace, Love, and Unity was born.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>Upon looking back, I learnt a lot of things.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>National anthems are about becoming one with the people, on the land we share.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>The ways of expressing may take different songs,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>May take different languages;
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>May take different genres;
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>But in the end,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>It's all the same thing.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>We sing in harmony,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>Upon the land we stand on,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>For the achievements of our ancestors,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>For them,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>For us,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>For all of our souls as one,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>To have Peace, Love, and Unity."</credit-words>
  </credit>
  <credit page="1">
    <credit-type>composer</credit-type>
    <credit-words default-x="1134.19" default-y="1526.67" justify="right" valign="bottom" font-size="12">-Kiro- a.k.a. Cheong Po Yao</credit-words>
  </credit>
  <credit page="2">
    <credit-words default-x="56.6929" default-y="1643.78" justify="left" valign="top" font-weight="bold" font-size="17">There are a few things that I wish to specify, before you play this medley.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-weight="normal" font-size="12">1. This medley contains 208 national anthems of 194 recognized countries, and 9 unofficial countries.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>2. 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>(to be changed upon completion)
</credit-words>
    <credit-words> The only country(s) that is(are) not included is(are):
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="10">The Islamic State of Iraq and Syria (ISIS) (due to obvious controversies and no sheet music)
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>Kyrgyzstan (no sheet music)
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>South Sudan (no sheet music)
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="12">3. If your country, anthem has lower volume than others (
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-family="MScore Text">
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-family="FreeSerif"> or 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-family="MScore Text">
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-family="FreeSerif">), it's generally for musical effect, instead of 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>a lack of affection for the countries.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>4. I started this project at 23rd October, 2015 when I was 14. 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>5. If you country's anthem starts at a weird transition (i.e. halfway through the chorus or verse), feel free to 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>contact me on the MuseScore page you downloaded this sheet music.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>6. This composition is free for anyone to use. Just credit me if you use it. But:
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="10">I: Do not add lyrics/edit this and republish.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>II: Do not upload this to YouTube. I'l be the one doing that.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>III: Give credit if you covered this. (also feel free to post a link at the MuseScore page!)
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>IV: If you want a full cover of your anthem, comment and I'll -try to- make it.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="12">7. This medley is around two hours long. Play at own risk! :O
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>8. Special thanks to my overseas and local friends:
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="10">I: Josh Chi Bonifacio "Jawshy" Ocaya, Angelo "Gelo" Allanza, and Charlene "Char" Franco from Philippines;
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>II: Marisa June "Mari" Black (girlfriend &lt;3), Anthony "Tony" Singleton, Jack R. Bennett, Zachary Daniels, Josh Smith, and 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>     Tyler Huffman from the United States of America;
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>III: Laura Cassandra "Larry" Vesselgaard from Denmark;
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>IV: Bodonea Valentina Zenobiu "Tina" Renate from Romania;
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>V: "Jason" T. Zhi Xian , "Sally Purple" Y. Hui Shan , Shania A. , "Natsu" L. Jun Heng , Benoit P. , "Butter" L. You Sheng , 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>     C. Ming Zhao , my family, and all my other friends from Malaysia.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="12">9. Also, special thanks to MuseScore.org (and the MuseScore community at MuseScore.com, of course!), 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>MidiWorld.com, MayaSite.net, Tabs-Ultimate-Guitar.com (chords), Cantorion.org, NationalAnthems.info, 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>ScoreExchange.com, Hamie.net, and PortaleStoria.net for providing sheet music. 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="10">(full credits in Excel file to be added)
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="12">10. Also, special thanks to Wikipedia.org and NationalAnthems.info for providing information.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>11. Denmark has 2 national anthems: "There is a Lovely Country" at 120 BPM and D Major; 
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>and "King Christian Stood by the Lofty Mast" at 100 BPM and G Major.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>12: Due to file size causing corruptions, Part I only has the following songs:
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="11">Hungary, Switzerland, Sweden, Portugal, USA, Haiti, Serbia, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Paraguay, Venezuela, Norway,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>Argentina, Costa Rica, El Salvador, Greece, Guatemala, Honduras, Nicaragua, Peru, Brazil, Ecuador, Bolivia, Uruguay,
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>Belgium, Dominican Republic, Liberia, Denmark, Canada, Romania, Philippines, Cuba, Panama, Bulgaria, Mongolia.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words font-size="12">13: Feel free to make sheet music of this for orchestras, as long as you credit me.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>14: There are a few languages which cannot be displayed due to them being not supported on standard
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>computers. I am terribly sorry, but I have tried to put transliterations for them.
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>
</credit-words>
    <credit-words>15: Just assume every bar has a pedal mkay &lt;3
</credit-words>
    <credit-words />
  </credit>
